{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-avft",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.78, Phase 6. `project-avft`: `project-hotelling`'s links and off-network fleet over a NON-DEFAULT avft (`inputs/washtenaw-project-avft.esm`, the same stated rows as `scale-county-avft`). The passenger car's (21) gasoline, diesel and electric and the combination long-haul truck's (62) diesel and electric are selected (MOVES adds 21's E85 and 62's CNG: \"Added missing vehicle selection\"); Total Energy at running exhaust, extended idle and APU and NOx at running exhaust and extended idle. MOVESOutput is 489 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES beside `scale-county-avft`'s rewritten fleet (23 sample-vehicle rows of 21 and 62 here): ProjectTAG's hotellingHours, which multiply the off-network fleet by avft.fuelEngFraction READ DIRECTLY (`hot_avftTotal`). At model year 2018 the long-haul truck's avft rows sum to 0.99999994 -- a gasoline share sampleVehiclePopulation has no row for and an electric share inside the 1e-6 threshold included, MOVES writing a gasoline hotellingHours row for it -- while the rewritten fleet sums to 0.998217, so the DEFAULT path's `hot_stmyTotal` would be 0.18% low on that cohort's extended idle and APU (finding F88).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 489; `n_sourceBin` 4, the electric long-haul cohort's two drives times two regulatory classes; `n_physicsRow` 21. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain",
      "control-strategy",
      "avft"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
